# .trivyignore — baseline exceptions for the security CI gate.
#
# Every entry MUST carry:
#   - CVE / GHSA id
#   - owner team (per config/teams.yaml)
#   - expiry date (ISO 8601) — after this date the entry is auto-removed
#     and the gate fails if the CVE is still present
#   - rationale (which epic closes the CVE)
#
# Trivy parses this file by lines that start with a CVE/GHSA id; the rest
# is a comment. Use a stable comment syntax below.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN       YYYY-MM-DD  owner-team  rationale
#   GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx  YYYY-MM-DD  owner-team  rationale
#
# Owner of this file: @genealogy/security (per ownership-catalog.md §6.4).
# New entries require an ADR or an explicit security review approval.

